-- EXPECT-ERROR: Module `Array` does not export `lst_rev`.
mod Main do
  -- Widening slice 2, Task 4 -- selective `use X.{name}` of a PRIVATE name.
  -- `Array.lst_rev` is a real `pfn` (stdlib/array.march:39, the same
  -- function `reject/t26_cross_module_private_fn` exercises through plain
  -- qualified access). Because `Array` is spliced in as a real `DMod` before
  -- typecheck runs (`bin/main.ml`'s `load_stdlib`), `lst_rev` was already
  -- excluded from `pub_set` at the `DMod` export step (`typecheck.ml`
  -- ~6884-6927, per `core-march-types.md` §2.5) -- so "Array.lst_rev" was
  -- NEVER written into `env.vars` in the first place. `DUse`'s `UseNames`
  -- arm (~typecheck.ml:7320-7337) looks it up, misses, and raises "Module
  -- `%s` does not export `%s`." -- textually distinct from, but rooted in
  -- the EXACT SAME `pub_set` gate as, `reject/t26`'s "is private to module"
  -- message (the qualified-var-resolution path's `qualified_error_msg`
  -- phrasing for the same underlying absence). Confirms selective `use` is
  -- consistent with Task 1's cross-module visibility fix: a private name is
  -- unreachable through EITHER path, `use`-selector or bare qualification.
  use Array.{lst_rev}

  fn main() : Int do 0 end
end
